// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ch17 B11 "Ysolde's table" (C, 1.5 min, ~60 words). act3_ch17.md §2 B11;
// act3_threads T-04: Ama's keth give the COUNT (her lone question-knot is the eighth place); the Choir stones hold the
// melody in fragments and the Lamptongue WORDS; the tune is Pell's to teach (Ch18 K05). README rule 3: nobody sings.
title: ch17_ysoldes_table
location: ch17/hollowmere
---
@letterbox on
@camera D18
@mark ysolde fathers_table walk
@anim ysolde lay_out keth_cord
@wait 2.0
@anim ysolde lay_out stone_rubbings
@wait 2.0
@anim ysolde lay_out blank_page
@wait 2.0
Ysolde [neutral]: Ama's count. Seven houses, and a question-knot hanging at the end. The question is the eighth place. #line:ch17_table_001
Ysolde [neutral]: The words are cut in the Choir stones. Lamptongue. I can read Lamptongue. #line:ch17_table_002
@anim ysolde touch blank_page
@wait 2.0
Ysolde [neutral]: Words I can do. The tune isn't mine to learn. #line:ch17_table_003
<<if $ch12_ysolde_confessed>>
    Ysolde [soft_smile]: I counted wrong once, on purpose. Not this time. #line:ch17_table_004
<<endif>>
@wait 2.0
<<set $ch17_verse_begun = true>>
@letterbox off
===
